MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_001: Hah! Tyah! Hyah!
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_002: Oh, Promised One. Have I done something worthy of\nyour attention? Really, it was less than nothing.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_003: The enemy is already dead. There's no joy or\nsadness in their defeat.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_004: <NCA>"But you are smiling...a little."
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_005: Huh? Oh... So I am. I hadn't noticed.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_006: Maybe it's because it feels fulfilling, even enjoyable,\nto use my strength to tear down evil.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_007: Disgusting... It's wrong to delight in defeating foes,\nno matter how evil they are.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_008: Mm...
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_009: When I said things like that long ago, people told me\nI was admirable for being so idealistic.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_010: I disagree. History is full of idealists who went astray.\nToo many to count.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_011: <NCA>"Where did your ideals come from?"
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_012: My father. The first memory I have is of him.\nA knight on his steed, truly beloved by his people.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_013: I wanted to be just like that. I hoped I might become\nan ideal, honorable knight.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_014: I trained hard and entered the service, but the\ncountry I served was far from my ideal. So I left.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_015: Since then I've been a wandering mercenary.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_016: Ah. How silly of me to ramble. Apologies for my\nimmaturity.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_017: No need to comfort me. My father once told me\nI had a lot of growing up to do.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_018: My talk of ideals shows that I haven't grown up\nat all. I'm demanding, selfish, inflexible...
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_019: <NCA>"But your ideals put others first."
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_020: <NCB>"You strive to protect others. Who, exactly?"
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_021: <ACA>Of course. Above all else, a knight must put his\npeople first.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_022: <ACB>Isn't it obvious? I want to protect my people.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_023: I've always aspired to be the ideal knight, and\nsearched for a lord worthy of my service.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_024: But I've lost my way, as if I've been chasing nothing\nmore than a child's foolish dream.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_025: At my core, I do truly wish to serve others.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_026: I'm not driven by a desire to smite evil, but to\nbring happiness to everyone.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_A_027: I can't thank you enough, Promised One. You've\nrestored my resolve.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_001: Thanks to you, Promised One, this idealist is finally\ngoing to be a knight. If only you were here...
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_002: Huh? You're alive?! I...I can barely believe it.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_003: <NCA>"Are you...happy to see me?"
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_004: How could I not be happy? I'm just...surprised.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_005: While you were gone, I kept thinking about my\nfather, before he died.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_006: Whenever I told him I was ready to serve as a\nknight, he'd say, "It's too soon."
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_007: I wonder if he knew about the corruption in the\nkingdom of Arago.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_008: It's possible he gave his life in an attempt to stop that\nvery corruption.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_009: Ah...
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_010: Back then, Arago was just a mess. I didn't know that,\nof course.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_011: I only wanted to become a knight of virtue, so after\nmy father died, I stepped up. Then I saw the truth.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_012: It was like a darkness closing in. When I realized\nwhom I was serving, I ran away with Rocinan.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_013: Father was trying to stop me because he knew I\nwould falter.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_014: I abandoned my people to chase some dream, some\nprecious ideal. I regret that choice to this day.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_015: It's time for me to return to Arago. To go back to \nthe land my father protected, despite its corruption.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_016: <NCA>"That's a good plan."
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_017: <NCB>"Arago needs you."
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_018: <ACA>Promised One... Perhaps, well. Would you?
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_019: <ACB>I'm not sure about that, but perhaps you'd...maybe...
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_020: No. Never mind that. I go in service of my ideals.\nProtecting my people. Upholding the peace.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_021: You are called to the whole world's salvation. I'll go\nto my country. I doubt we'll meet again.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_022: <NCA>"I'll really miss you."
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_023: Huh. It's not like you to speak that way.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_024: <RSDS>Let us say this... Come to me in Arago, should you\never grow lonely. I vow to rid it of conflict.
MID_SE_Ism_Iio_S_025: It will be a land where all people can be happy\ntogether. A most...ideal place.